00:33:07.690 --> 00:33:09.810
FRANSESC CAMPOY:
Yeah, so the question

00:33:09.810 --> 00:33:14.685
regarding your pet peeve,
your favorite project.

00:33:14.685 --> 00:33:16.060
MARK MANDEL: My
favorite project?

00:33:16.060 --> 00:33:17.870
FRANSESC CAMPOY: Yeah,
Deployment Manager.

00:33:17.870 --> 00:33:20.224
And it's basically about,
OK, so Deployment Manager,

00:33:20.224 --> 00:33:21.640
basically what it
allows you to do

00:33:21.640 --> 00:33:24.350
is, given a file that
contains some description,

00:33:24.350 --> 00:33:27.220
you will create all the
resources on your Google Cloud

00:33:27.220 --> 00:33:28.830
Platform project.

00:33:28.830 --> 00:33:30.480
And that is cool.

00:33:30.480 --> 00:33:34.180
But is there any way
you can create that file

00:33:34.180 --> 00:33:35.750
from what you already have?

00:33:35.750 --> 00:33:41.750
Meaning that, via either the
CLI or the web interface,

00:33:41.750 --> 00:33:44.770
you created a bunch
of, I don't know,

00:33:44.770 --> 00:33:50.060
instances, cloud storage
buckets, and whatever,

00:33:50.060 --> 00:33:54.270
and you want to basically create
the corresponding Deployment

00:33:54.270 --> 00:33:56.000
Manager, so then
you can replicate

00:33:56.000 --> 00:33:59.140
that same infrastructure
somewhere else.

00:33:59.140 --> 00:34:01.680
MARK MANDEL: So as
of about 15 days ago,

00:34:01.680 --> 00:34:04.020
there is a beginning
of doing exactly that.

00:34:04.020 --> 00:34:06.570
I would say it's definitely
not, like, 100% there,

00:34:06.570 --> 00:34:09.090
but it's an open source project
that sits within the Google

00:34:09.090 --> 00:34:12.449
Cloud Platform Deployment
Manager samples repository,

00:34:12.449 --> 00:34:15.620
where there's a genconfig
Python script where you're

00:34:15.620 --> 00:34:19.060
able to point it, I think
primarily right now, at GCE

00:34:19.060 --> 00:34:21.159
instances, but hopefully
that will sort of grow

00:34:21.159 --> 00:34:23.920
from there, as we get
issues and pool requests,

00:34:23.920 --> 00:34:26.900
and be able to get back a
basic sort of Jinja template

00:34:26.900 --> 00:34:28.985
that's able to be used
with Deployment Manager.

00:34:28.985 --> 00:34:30.860
I think you'll have to
tweak it a little bit.

00:34:30.860 --> 00:34:33.365
But it definitely does a lot
of that bulk work for you,

00:34:33.365 --> 00:34:35.489
so that, if you want to
get started with Deployment

00:34:35.489 --> 00:34:37.719
Manager, but you've already
got some infrastructure,

00:34:37.719 --> 00:34:40.010
and you want basically be
able to either replicate that

00:34:40.010 --> 00:34:43.389
somewhere else, or maybe modify
